Developer affordances are a build flag, not a feature
====================================================

The key box and the door back into onboarding sat in the bottom-left of every build, in the same corner
a user looks at to find Settings. They exist to build the thing, not to be shipped with it, and a
published Flatpak must not have a paste-a-key-here box pretending to be part of the product.

The engine reads `QUIXI_DEVELOPER` from its environment and hands the shell a boolean; the shell
renders those two controls only when it is true. A build that sets nothing — the Flatpak, the package,
anything shipped — has neither in the DOM at all, not merely hidden.

Verified both directions in containers: without the variable the automation bridge reports no
Onboarding (development) control and no dev key field; with `QUIXI_DEVELOPER=1` both return.

